# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**A `svc-ai-litellm` gateway is the single model entrypoint.** It exposes one OpenAI-compatible `/v1` endpoint and routes to backends via its `model_list`. No consumer addresses a provider directly."
msgstr "**A `svc-ai-litellm` Digivärav on ühe mudeli sisendpunkt.** See paljastab ühe OpenAI- ga ühilduva `/v1` lõpp-punkt ja marsruudid taustaprogrammidesse selle kaudu `model_list`. Ükski tarbija ei pöördu otse teenusepakkuja poole."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**A `svc-ai-lmstudio` role is added as a routable backend, x86/GPU node only.** It deploys LM Studio in headless server mode (`lms server`, OpenAI-compatible API) and registers behind the gateway. LM Studio has no arm64 Linux server build, so it MUST be pinned to an x86 (typically GPU) node via placement constraint and MUST NOT be scheduled onto the Raspberry Pi / arm64 agent nodes of [032](032-agent-employees-firecracker.md). LM Studio ships primarily as a desktop GUI; the role MUST use its headless/server mode, and the README MUST document the container caveat (GPU passthrough, licensing/model-download constraints)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**A change in `services.hugo.source_version`** invalidates the clone, which invalidates `COPY ./services/repository/` in the Dockerfile, which triggers a fresh `hugo` build on the next deploy."
msgstr "**Muutus `services.hugo.source_version`** Tühistab klooni, mis muudab selle kehtetuks `COPY ./services/repository/` Dockerfile, mis käivitab värske `hugo` arendame edasi järgmist tegevust."

msgid "**A cluster dump is replayed, not skipped.** The recover chain sends it through `baudolo-restore cluster` with the superuser of its cluster row, so a generation holding one proves that instance restorable like any other dump; a missing cluster row is a red, not a silent skip."
msgstr ""

msgid "**A collector on every server host.** A host-level `sys-*` collector role runs in the server stage loop (`tasks/stages/02_server.yml`) on every server host, including the NFS and backup hosts, reads journald and pushes to Loki through an authenticated endpoint with a tenant header. The ingest endpoint is never served on an onion address. The containers of the collector, Loki and Grafana are not ingested again."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**A declared window is an upper bound the backend honours, and the token demand is a floor.** Two numbers guard the same decision from opposite sides, and each was wrong in the direction that hid the other. `smollm2:135m` was declared at 16384 against a trained `max_position_embeddings` of 8192 with no rope scaling, so Ollama clamped `num_ctx` and then truncated the prompt to half the window, which is the `n_left=4091` recorded in `8dbdd31b22`. Meanwhile `CHARS_PER_TOKEN = 3` was justified as erring high, but the router's own probe builds its oversized prompt from `\"x \"`, which tokenizes at two characters per token: 16384 characters are 8193 real tokens on all three served tokenizers against an estimate of 5461."
msgstr "**Deklareeritud aken on taustaprogrammi autasude ülemine sidumine ja sümboolne nõue on põrand.** Kaks numbrit kaitsevad sama otsust vastaskülgedelt ja kumbki eksis suunas, mis peitis teise. `smollm2:135m` kuulutati 16384 treenitud `max_position_embeddings` ühest 8192 ilma köieta, nii et Ollama klammerdatud `num_ctx` Ja siis kärbiti viipa poole aknani, mis on `n_left=4091` salvestatud `8dbdd31b22`. Vahepeal. `CHARS_PER_TOKEN = 3` oli põhjendatud, et viga on kõrge, kuid ruuteri enda sond ehitab oma ülisuurt kiirust `\"x \"`, mis tähistab kahte märki märgi kohta: 16384 tegelased 8193 Reaalsed märgid kõigi kolme serveeritud tokenizers vastu hinnanguline 5461."

msgid "**A dedicated role, not Stalwart config.** Stalwart has no outbound SOCKS support ([stalwartlabs/stalwart#644](https://github.com/stalwartlabs/stalwart/issues/644)), so the Tor hop lives in a separate service that only the `.onion` route uses."
msgstr ""

msgid "**A dedicated role, not Stalwart config.** Stalwart has no outbound SOCKS support (`stalwartlabs/stalwart#644 <https://github.com/stalwartlabs/stalwart/issues/644>`__), so the Tor hop lives in a separate service that only the ``.onion`` route uses."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**A dump needs a running engine.** It is replayed through ``docker exec``, so unlike a file tree it cannot be restored onto a bare host. After a total loss the order is: deploy the stack, stop the consumers, replay, start them again. The step names which of the two states is missing — a stopped container that only needs starting, or no container at all."
msgstr "**Prügila vajab töötavat mootorit.** See mängitakse uuesti läbi ``docker exec``, nii et erinevalt failipuust ei saa seda taastada paljale hostile. Pärast täielikku kaotust on järjekord järgmine: juurutage virna, peatage tarbijad, mängige uuesti, käivitage need uuesti. Sammide nimed, mis kahest riigist puuduvad - peatatud konteiner, mis vajab ainult käivitamist või üldse mitte konteinerit."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**A dump needs a running engine.** It is replayed through `docker exec`, so unlike a file tree it cannot be restored onto a bare host. After a total loss the order is: deploy the stack, stop the consumers, replay, start them again. The step names which of the two states is missing — a stopped container that only needs starting, or no container at all."
msgstr "**Prügila vajab töötavat mootorit.** See mängitakse uuesti läbi `docker exec`, nii et erinevalt failipuust ei saa seda taastada paljale hostile. Pärast täielikku kaotust on järjekord järgmine: juurutage virna, peatage tarbijad, mängige uuesti, käivitage need uuesti. Sammide nimed, mis kahest riigist puuduvad - peatatud konteiner, mis vajab ainult käivitamist või üldse mitte konteinerit."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**A force rebuild** without a source-version change can be triggered by clearing the role's image cache:"
msgstr "**Jõudude taastamine** ilma lähteversiooni muutmiseta saab käivitada rolli pildi vahemälu puhastamisega:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**A probe for every container.** Health checks are composed from prefixes and are mandatory: every declared image either carries a probe or states why it cannot have one, enforced from both sides. Probes hit the port the container actually binds, no longer derive an HTTP Host from a kernel hostname, and are defined once instead of per proxy. Rescue diagnostics pin the dnsmasq listener loss to its moment, sample what the resolver answers rather than just its socket, probe the daemon.json upstreams, and record the whole boot instead of the last 10 000 lines."
msgstr "**Sondi iga konteineri jaoks.** Tervisekontrollid koosnevad eesliidetest ja on kohustuslikud: iga deklareeritud kujutis kannab kas sondi või märgib, miks seda ei saa, jõustades mõlemalt poolt. Sondid tabavad porti, mida konteiner tegelikult seob, ei tuleta enam HTTP hosti kerneli hostinimest ja määratletakse üks kord proksi asemel. Päästediagnostika kinnitab dnsmasqi kuulaja kaotuse oma hetkeni, proovib, mida lahendaja vastab, mitte ainult selle pesa, sondib daemon.json ülesvoolu ja salvesta kogu saapa viimase asemel 10 000 jooned."

msgid "**A refusal re-asks the next engine instead of ending the request.** Decision 11 rejects an answer that mangles a protected term. That verdict is about one engine's answer for one language pair, not about the string being untranslatable, because a refusal class is a property of the engine *and* the pair. The gateway therefore offers the same request to the next candidate of the set decision 5 ranked, minus the engines that already refused it, and returns the first answer that survives the check. Only when every candidate has refused does the gateway report the refusal, and never a mangled translation."
msgstr ""

msgid "**A request stays inside the deployment while a local model can serve it.** A prompt can carry a credential, so locality is its own rank above price rather than a consequence of local models happening to be free. `services.litellm.router.remote_fallback` defaults to `false`: while any local route is deployed, a request no local model can take is refused with its reason instead of reaching a third party, and the refusal names the switch that would allow it. With no local route deployed the rule does not apply, because there would be nothing to hold the request on."
msgstr ""

msgid "**A reviewed human translation outranks every engine.** The gateway consults Weblate's translation memory first; a string with a reviewed translation is returned verbatim, no engine is called, and machine output MUST NOT overwrite it. This is the only hard precedence rule in the gateway."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**A role may narrow the pool.** `meta/services.yml.<primary_entity> .architectures` lists what the role can run on, next to `modes`, because both state a capability rather than a testing preference. The row draws from the intersection of the run's pool with the declarations of the role and of every role the deploy planner brings up for that variant, because the deploy pulls those in too; an empty intersection aborts the matrix."
msgstr "**Roll võib basseini kitsendada.** `meta/services.yml.<primary_entity> .architectures` Loetleb, mis rolli saab mängida kõrval `modes`, sest mõlemad on pigem võime kui testimiseelistus. Rida joonistab jooksu basseini ristumiskohast rolli ja iga rolli deklaratsioonidega, mida juurutamise planeerija selle variandi jaoks esitab, sest juurutamine tõmbab ka neid; tühi ristmik katkestab maatriksi."

msgid "**A service flag in the row role's `meta/services.yml`.** The infinito-native integrations are plain service keys — `sso` (keycloak), `matomo`, `prometheus`, `email` (mailu), `dashboard`, `css`, `logout`, `cdn`, `coturn`, `collabora`, `onlyoffice`, `libretranslate` and `litellm`. Each is group-gated, so the flag tells you both that the integration exists and when it is active. `lookup('roles_with_service', '<key>')` answers \"who consumes this\" from the repository itself; no second list needs to agree with it."
msgstr ""

# ulatumist rakenduskiht ei kontrolli.** Komponendi virnal, Flowise ja Baserow
# ühineme `postgres` kuna mõlemad kasutavad keskandmebaasi ja Flowise avaneb
# `baserow:80` kell `192.168.200.5` kuigi Baserow ei tunnista Flowise.Reach
# tuleb mõõta määratud aadressiga: tundmatu nimi langeb metamärgi lahendajale,
# kes vastab ühe ligipääsetava aadressiga, nii et nimepõhine sondi teatab
# igast eakaaslasest kui ligipääsetavast ja ei tõesta midagi.
# gained=['Flowise.Reach']
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**A shared infrastructure network carries lateral reach the application layer does not control.** On the compose stack, Flowise and Baserow both join `postgres` because both use the central database, and Flowise opens `baserow:80` at `192.168.200.5` although Baserow does not admit Flowise. Reach has to be measured by resolved address: an unknown name falls through to a wildcard resolver that answers with one reachable address, so a name-based probe reports every peer as reachable and proves nothing."
msgstr "**Jagatud infrastruktuurivõrk kannab külgsuunalist ulatumist rakenduskiht ei kontrolli.** Komponendi virnal, Flowise ja Baserow ühineme `postgres` kuna mõlemad kasutavad keskandmebaasi ja Flowise avaneb `baserow:80` kell `192.168.200.5` kuigi Baserow ei tunnista Flowise.Reach tuleb mõõta määratud aadressiga: tundmatu nimi langeb metamärgi lahendajale, kes vastab ühe ligipääsetava aadressiga, nii et nimepõhine sondi teatab igast eakaaslasest kui ligipääsetavast ja ei tõesta midagi."

