#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Break-glass local admin:** `SEMAPHORE_ADMIN*` seeds a local admin from the `web-app-semaphore-breakglass` user in every variant. With the `native` method on it signs in through the login form. With SSO on the form is hidden, and the account signs in through the login API, which `SEMAPHORE_PASSWORD_LOGIN_DISABLED` leaves open: `POST /api/auth/login` with `{\"auth\": \"<username>\", \"password\": \"<password>\"}` sets the session cookie, after which the UI opens signed in. With the `ldap` method on the account cannot sign in."
