msgid "**Read-only IdP fields:** ``services.sso.profile.locked`` decides which fields are locked. ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ renders its keys into ``WORDPRESS_OIDC_PROFILE_LOCKED``. On ``profile.php`` and ``user-edit.php`` of an OIDC account those fields are read-only with a translated warning as their hover title, rendered by the shared lock renderer of ``sys-front-inj-javascript``. Every write through ``wp_insert_user`` (the profile and user forms, ``/wp/v2/users``, XML-RPC ``wp.editProfile``, any plugin calling ``wp_update_user``) keeps their stored values, except the profile sync of the OIDC login itself. Removing a key unlocks its field in the form and on every write; the next OIDC login still overwrites it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Read-only IdP fields:** `services.sso.profile.locked` decides which fields are locked. [`templates/env.j2`](./templates/env.j2) renders its keys into `JOOMLA_OIDC_PROFILE_LOCKED`, and for an SSO account the plugin renders exactly those fields read-only in the com_users profile form and keeps their stored values when a profile save carries others. `onUserBeforeSave` refuses every other change of a locked field or of the SSO marker of an SSO account from a site request or from the web services API. The shared lock renderer of `sys-front-inj-javascript` adds the translated warning to the same fields as their hover title. Removing a key unlocks its field in the form and on save; the next login still overwrites it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Read-only IdP fields:** `services.sso.profile.locked` decides which fields are locked. [`templates/env.j2`](./templates/env.j2) renders its keys into `WORDPRESS_OIDC_PROFILE_LOCKED`. On `profile.php` and `user-edit.php` of an OIDC account those fields are read-only with a translated warning as their hover title, rendered by the shared lock renderer of `sys-front-inj-javascript`. Every write through `wp_insert_user` (the profile and user forms, `/wp/v2/users`, XML-RPC `wp.editProfile`, any plugin calling `wp_update_user`) keeps their stored values, except the profile sync of the OIDC login itself. Removing a key unlocks its field in the form and on every write; the next OIDC login still overwrites it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Read-only IdP fields:** every Keycloak login overwrites name, email and username. For an OAuth account Grafana renders the three profile fields disabled and refuses `PUT /api/user` and `PUT /api/users/:id` with HTTP 403 (`Cannot update external User`). The fields are declared in `services.sso.profile.locked`; the shared lock renderer of `sys-front-inj-javascript` adds the translated warning as their hover title in one of the UI languages listed in `services.sso.profile.languages`, and `files/playwright/test-profile-lock.js` proves both. The selectors match every disabled profile field, and Grafana also disables them for a local account while `native` is off; the break-glass account then has no UI session, because the login form is gone."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Read-only IdP fields:** every Keycloak login overwrites name, email and username. For an OAuth account Grafana renders the three profile fields disabled and refuses ``PUT /api/user`` and ``PUT /api/users/:id`` with HTTP 403 (``Cannot update external User``). The fields are declared in ``services.sso.profile.locked``; the shared lock renderer of ``sys-front-inj-javascript`` adds the translated warning as their hover title in one of the UI languages listed in ``services.sso.profile.languages``, and ``files/playwright/test-profile-lock.js`` proves both. The selectors match every disabled profile field, and Grafana also disables them for a local account while ``native`` is off; the break-glass account then has no UI session, because the login form is gone."
