msgid "**Restricted sign-in:** With SSO, the gateway sets ``general_settings.ui_access_mode`` to ``restricted_sso_group`` on the ``web-app-litellm`` administrator group path in the groups claim, so the SSO login refuses every other Keycloak account with ``403`` before LiteLLM stores a user row; a refused login takes none of the five free SSO seats."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted sign-in:** With SSO, the gateway sets `general_settings.ui_access_mode` to `restricted_sso_group` on the `web-app-litellm` administrator group path in the groups claim, so the SSO login refuses every other Keycloak account with `403` before LiteLLM stores a user row; a refused login takes none of the five free SSO seats."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retention and redaction.** Retention is an inventory parameter per log class with a default of 7 days. Secrets are redacted at the source where an application emits them and again in a central pipeline stage; a canary test proves that a synthetic secret never reaches Loki. The 200-line log excerpt that `sys-ctl-hlth-container` sends with its alerts is redacted by the same rules."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retention per log class:** ``services.loki.retention`` maps each log class the collector assigns (``access``, ``application``, ``system``, ``security``) to a duration (``<n>h``, ``<n>d`` or ``<n>w``, at least ``24h``), 7 days by default. The ``loki_retention`` filter turns the map into one ``retention_stream`` per class; the compactor deletes older lines."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retention per log class:** `services.loki.retention` maps each log class the collector assigns (`access`, `application`, `system`, `security`) to a duration (`<n>h`, `<n>d` or `<n>w`, at least `24h`), 7 days by default. The `loki_retention` filter turns the map into one `retention_stream` per class; the compactor deletes older lines."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retention:** Finished, failed and cancelled renders are removed after a configurable number of days."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retired Units:** The weekly hard repair, which ran ``compose down`` and ``up -d`` on every instance, is gone. Each host that still carries its timer, service or script stops, disables and deletes them on its next deploy, before the destructor unlocks the timers again. ``sys-ctl-rpr-container-soft`` restarts a project with an unhealthy or exited container instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retired Units:** The weekly hard repair, which ran `compose down` and `up -d` on every instance, is gone. Each host that still carries its timer, service or script stops, disables and deletes them on its next deploy, before the destructor unlocks the timers again. `sys-ctl-rpr-container-soft` restarts a project with an unhealthy or exited container instead."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Retry-with-backoff:** transient SSH/rsync failures retry up to twelve times across a long window before surfacing as a hard failure."
msgstr "**Tagasilöögiga katse:** mööduvad SSH / rsync tõrked proovivad pikas aknas kuni kaksteist korda, enne kui pinnatakse kõva rikkena."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reusable Role:** Can be used as a foundational component for software development, CI/CD pipelines, and build environments."
msgstr "**Korduvkasutatav roll:** Seda saab kasutada tarkvaraarenduse, CI / CD torujuhtmete ja keskkonna ehitamise põhikomponendina."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reusable dependency role** for higher-level SSH workflows"
msgstr "**Korduvkasutatav sõltuvusfunktsioon** SSH kõrgema taseme töövoogude puhul"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Revalidation required:** [ADR 0003 - One MCP surface per provider, and a disposition for every role](../architecture/decisions/0003-mcp-surface-per-provider.md) holds the exhaustive per-role audit and the standing contract, and supersedes this document where this document assumes an empty baseline, treats metadata as enforcement, or marks client provisioning and end-to-end authorization complete. The remaining work is tracked in [035 - MCP Proxy Expansion and Application Interconnection](035-mcp-proxy-expansion.md). Checked items below describe the original implementation slice and MUST NOT be read as proof that the stricter identity, revocation, transport, restart, proxy, and real-tool-call criteria in requirement 035 are complete."
msgstr "**Pikendamine on nõutav:** [ADR 0003 Üks MCP pind pakkuja kohta ja jaotus iga rolli kohta](../architecture/decisions/0003-mcp-surface-per-provider.md) omab ammendavat rollipõhist auditit ja püsilepingut ning asendab selle dokumendi juhul, kui see dokument eeldab tühja lähtejoont, käsitleb metaandmeid jõustamisena või märgib kliendi varustamise ja otsast lõpuni autoriseerimise täielikuks. Ülejäänud tööd jälgitakse [035 MCP puhverserveri laiendamine ja rakenduste ühendamine](035-mcp-proxy-expansion.md). Allpool märgitud elemendid kirjeldavad algset rakenduslõiku ja EI TOHI lugeda tõendina selle kohta, et nõudes on rangemad identsus-, tühistamis-, transpordi-, taaskäivitus-, asendus- ja reaaltööriista-kõne kriteeriumid. 035 on valmis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reverse Proxy**"
msgstr "**Pöördproks**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reverse Proxy**   Includes the `sys-stk-front-proxy` role to configure a proxy (e.g. NGINX) for routing HTTP(S) traffic to your database UI or management endpoint."
msgstr "**Pöördproks** Sisaldab `sys-stk-front-proxy` puhverserveri seadistamise roll (nt NGINX) HTTP marsruutimiseks(S) liiklus teie andmebaasi UI või halduse lõpp-punkti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reverse bridge ownership (ActivityPub → AT).** Writing an AT record requires *an account to write it as*. Whose PDS, whose app-password/OAuth token? Options: a dedicated service account, or per-user delegated write via the login-broker. Unresolved → reverse direction deferred to a follow-up requirement."
msgstr "**Pöördsilla omandiõigus (ActivityPub → AT).** AT-kirje kirjutamine nõuab *konto selle kirjutamiseks*Kelle PDS, kelle app-password/OAuth token? Valikud: spetsiaalne teenusekonto või kasutaja kohta delegeeritud kirjutamine sisselogimisvahendaja kaudu. Lahendamata → vastupidine suund on edasi lükatud järelmeetmete nõudeks."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reverse-Proxy Ready:** Sets `ATL_PROXY_NAME/PORT/SCHEME/SECURE` so Confluence generates correct external URLs behind HTTPS."
msgstr "**Pöörd-Proxy Ready:** Määrab `ATL_PROXY_NAME/PORT/SCHEME/SECURE` Confluence genereerib HTTPS-i taga õigeid väliseid URL-e."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reverse-Proxy Ready:** Sets ``ATL_PROXY_NAME/PORT/SCHEME/SECURE`` so Confluence generates correct external URLs behind HTTPS."
msgstr "**Pöörd-Proxy Ready:** Määrab ``ATL_PROXY_NAME/PORT/SCHEME/SECURE`` Confluence genereerib HTTPS-i taga õigeid väliseid URL-e."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reverse-Proxy/HTTPS Ready:** Preconfigured Atlassian Tomcat proxy envs so Jira respects external scheme/host/port."
msgstr "**Pöörd-Proksü/HTTPS Valmis:** Eelkonfigureeritud Atlassian Tomcat proxy envs, nii et Jira austab väliseid scheme/host/port."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reverse-proxy trust:** Renders a ``configuration.yaml`` with ``default_config``, ``use_x_forwarded_for``, and the project-wide trusted-proxy CIDRs listed in ``trusted_proxies``. In swarm the hub joins the proxy’s own overlay, so the forwarded request arrives from that network rather than from the hub’s, and trusting only the hub’s subnet makes Home Assistant answer every proxied request with HTTP 400."
msgstr "**Pöördproksi usaldus:** Renders ``configuration.yaml`` koos ``default_config``, ``use_x_forwarded_for``, ja kogu projekti hõlmavaid usaldusväärseid CIDRe, mis on loetletud ``trusted_proxies``. sülemis ühineb jaotur puhverserveri enda kattega, nii et edastatud päring saabub sellest võrgust, mitte jaoturi alamvõrgust, ja usaldades ainult jaoturi alamvõrku, vastab Home Assistant igale HTTP-ga esitatud päringule 400."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reverse-proxy trust:** Renders a `configuration.yaml` with `default_config`, `use_x_forwarded_for`, and the project-wide trusted-proxy CIDRs listed in `trusted_proxies`. In swarm the hub joins the proxy's own overlay, so the forwarded request arrives from that network rather than from the hub's, and trusting only the hub's subnet makes Home Assistant answer every proxied request with HTTP 400."
msgstr "**Pöördproksi usaldus:** Renders `configuration.yaml` koos `default_config`, `use_x_forwarded_for`, ja kogu projekti hõlmavaid usaldusväärseid CIDRe, mis on loetletud `trusted_proxies`. sülemis ühineb jaotur puhverserveri enda kattega, nii et edastatud päring saabub sellest võrgust, mitte jaoturi alamvõrgust, ja ainult jaoturi alamvõrgu usaldamine paneb Home Assistanti vastama igale HTTP-ga prokseeritud päringule 400."

msgid "**Reverse-proxy trust:** ``gateway.trustedProxies`` carries only the address space the front proxy connects from: the role subnet pool (``NETWORK_ROLE_SUBNET_POOL``) in compose mode, where the proxy reaches the published port through a role network gateway, and Docker’s default overlay pool in swarm mode. Loopback and the other private ranges are no longer trusted. Without the proxy’s source the gateway answers a Control UI WebSocket that arrives with forwarded headers with ``trusted_proxy_untrusted_source`` and closes it before the pairing step, which the Control UI reports as a network failure rather than as a pairing prompt."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Reverse-proxy trust:** `gateway.trustedProxies` carries only the address space the front proxy connects from: the role subnet pool (`NETWORK_ROLE_SUBNET_POOL`) in compose mode, where the proxy reaches the published port through a role network gateway, and Docker's default overlay pool in swarm mode. Loopback and the other private ranges are no longer trusted. Without the proxy's source the gateway answers a Control UI WebSocket that arrives with forwarded headers with `trusted_proxy_untrusted_source` and closes it before the pairing step, which the Control UI reports as a network failure rather than as a pairing prompt."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Review gallery.** Each role gets its own private Artifact with at least 20 views, each captured in light and dark mode and in a desktop (1440×900) and a mobile (390×844) viewport, so at least 80 screenshots of the designed state per role. The views favour detail-rich surfaces: settings, administration, forms, lists and detail pages, logged in where the app has accounts, with idempotently seeded showcase content where a list or detail page would otherwise be empty. `make design-gallery app=<role>` captures them in one spec run and copies them to `/tmp/design-gallery/<role>/`. A comparison with the app before the design is captured on request only: `before=true` adds every view with every injected snippet stripped from the document (the body filter wraps its injections in `<!--infinito-inj-->` markers). The operator approves or rejects by comment."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Review workflow:** a translation becomes authoritative when a reviewer approves it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Review:** the review page shows the requester, the application, each requested role with its group path, the reason, and the requester's live groups. The approver can deselect roles before confirming."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Review:** the review page shows the requester, the application, each requested role with its group path, the reason, and the requester’s live groups. The approver can deselect roles before confirming."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Reviewed strings win:** a string approved in [`web-app-weblate`](../web-app-weblate/) is returned verbatim and no engine is called."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Reviewed strings win:** a string approved in ```web-app-weblate`` <../web-app-weblate/>`__ is returned verbatim and no engine is called."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Revoke a host:** clear its ``gateway_host``, re-run the pass and deploy the gateway host. The pass drops the host’s URL, model and key, and the gateway deletes every ``host:`` key no consuming host holds any more."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Revoke a host:** clear its `gateway_host`, re-run the pass and deploy the gateway host. The pass drops the host's URL, model and key, and the gateway deletes every `host:` key no consuming host holds any more."
