msgid "**Role-Based Access Control & Security:** Manage user permissions precisely to ensure that sensitive information and critical functions remain secure."
msgstr "**Rollipõhine juurdepääsu kontroll ja turvalisus:** Halda kasutaja õigusi just selleks, et tagada tundliku teabe ja kriitiliste funktsioonide turvalisus."

msgid "**Role-Based Sign-In:** Only members of a role group of [`meta/rbac.yml`](./meta/rbac.yml) sign in, through Keycloak (groups claim) and through the directory (`memberOf`) alike: `administrator` grants Settings, `manager` the Sales, Accounting, Inventory and Project administrator rights, `user` the internal user, `portal` the customer portal only (`ODOO_RBAC_ROLE_GROUPS` in [`vars/main.yml`](./vars/main.yml)). Every sign-in replaces these managed groups with the ones the roles grant; the platform administrator is never changed or refused. The addons [`infinito_rbac`](./files/addons/infinito_rbac/__manifest__.py), [`auth_oauth_https`](./files/addons/auth_oauth_https/__manifest__.py) and [`auth_ldap_profile`](./files/addons/auth_ldap_profile/__manifest__.py) under `files/addons/` carry the mapping."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Role-Based Sign-In:** Only members of a role group of ```meta/rbac.yml`` <./meta/rbac.yml>`__ sign in, through Keycloak (groups claim) and through the directory (``memberOf``) alike: ``administrator`` grants Settings, ``manager`` the Sales, Accounting, Inventory and Project administrator rights, ``user`` the internal user, ``portal`` the customer portal only (``ODOO_RBAC_ROLE_GROUPS`` in ```vars/main.yml`` <./vars/main.yml>`__). Every sign-in replaces these managed groups with the ones the roles grant; the platform administrator is never changed or refused. The addons ```infinito_rbac`` <./files/addons/infinito_rbac/__manifest__.py>`__, ```auth_oauth_https`` <./files/addons/auth_oauth_https/__manifest__.py>`__ and ```auth_ldap_profile`` <./files/addons/auth_ldap_profile/__manifest__.py>`__ under ``files/addons/`` carry the mapping."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Role-Group Sign-In:** [`files/php/oidc/role_gate.php`](./files/php/oidc/role_gate.php), mounted at `src/InfinitoRbac/AdminOpenAuthRoleGate.php` and registered in [`templates/adminopenauth.yaml.j2`](./templates/adminopenauth.yaml.j2) as a listener of AdminOpenAuth's `UserRedirectReceivedEvent` after the rule execution, answers `403` to a Keycloak sign-in that no role-assignment rule granted the admin flag or an ACL role. Shopware creates no account for such a user."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Role-Group Sign-In:** ```files/php/oidc/role_gate.php`` <./files/php/oidc/role_gate.php>`__, mounted at ``src/InfinitoRbac/AdminOpenAuthRoleGate.php`` and registered in ```templates/adminopenauth.yaml.j2`` <./templates/adminopenauth.yaml.j2>`__ as a listener of AdminOpenAuth’s ``UserRedirectReceivedEvent`` after the rule execution, answers ``403`` to a Keycloak sign-in that no role-assignment rule granted the admin flag or an ACL role. Shopware creates no account for such a user."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Role-Group Sign-In:** every deploy installs the module `InfinitoRbac` ([`group_user_provider.php`](./files/php/rbac/group_user_provider.php), [`binding.php`](./files/php/rbac/binding.php)) into `custom/Espo/Modules`, which replaces EspoCRM's OIDC user provider. A Keycloak sign-in without the `administrator`, `manager` or `user` group of this application is refused before EspoCRM creates an account, and an existing administrator account of such a user becomes a regular user. Each admitted sign-in sets the user type from the groups claim: `administrator` group members become EspoCRM administrators, every other member a regular user. The platform administrator signs in without a group and keeps its type. With LDAP only, the module's sign-in hook [`ldap_role_groups.php`](./files/php/rbac/ldap_role_groups.php) (`onSuccessHookClassNameList`) reads the account's `memberOf` from the directory at every password sign-in and applies the teams and user type `rbac.php` would set, so an account the LDAP login creates, or whose role groups changed, reaches its CRM records in that session instead of after the next RBAC run. When the directory cannot be read, the account keeps its teams and type until that run."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Role-Group Sign-In:** every deploy installs the module ``InfinitoRbac`` (```group_user_provider.php`` <./files/php/rbac/group_user_provider.php>`__, ```binding.php`` <./files/php/rbac/binding.php>`__) into ``custom/Espo/Modules``, which replaces EspoCRM’s OIDC user provider. A Keycloak sign-in without the ``administrator``, ``manager`` or ``user`` group of this application is refused before EspoCRM creates an account, and an existing administrator account of such a user becomes a regular user. Each admitted sign-in sets the user type from the groups claim: ``administrator`` group members become EspoCRM administrators, every other member a regular user. The platform administrator signs in without a group and keeps its type. With LDAP only, the module’s sign-in hook ```ldap_role_groups.php`` <./files/php/rbac/ldap_role_groups.php>`__ (``onSuccessHookClassNameList``) reads the account’s ``memberOf`` from the directory at every password sign-in and applies the teams and user type ``rbac.php`` would set, so an account the LDAP login creates, or whose role groups changed, reaches its CRM records in that session instead of after the next RBAC run. When the directory cannot be read, the account keeps its teams and type until that run."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Role-Restricted Directory Sign-In:** `LDAP_PROVIDER_FILTER` and `LDAP_QUERY_STRING` admit only members of the `administrator` and `user` role groups (`SUITECRM_LDAP_LOGIN_FILTER` in [`vars/main.yml`](./vars/main.yml))."
