msgid "A member of ``site-owner`` administers the site ``<username>.<parent>``, where ``domains.served`` in the Multisite variant sets the parent to ``user.blog.<DOMAIN_PRIMARY>``. Only a Keycloak username (``[a-z1-9]``, or the agent form ``<4 chars>0<suffix>``) of at most 63 characters that is no WordPress ``illegal_names`` entry names a site. The mapper creates the site on the member’s first SSO login, records the member’s OIDC subject on it and only ever takes over or archives a site that carries that subject or that the deploy reserved for the login. An SSO login outside the group archives the site and keeps its content, a login back in the group restores it. A deploy applies a membership change as well: `tasks/05_site_owners.yml <tasks/05_site_owners.yml>`__ archives every own site whose login is no longer an inventory member and ends that member’s sessions."
msgstr ""

msgid "A member of `site-owner` administers the site `<username>.<parent>`, where `domains.served` in the Multisite variant sets the parent to `user.blog.<DOMAIN_PRIMARY>`. Only a Keycloak username (`[a-z1-9]`, or the agent form `<4 chars>0<suffix>`) of at most 63 characters that is no WordPress `illegal_names` entry names a site. The mapper creates the site on the member's first SSO login, records the member's OIDC subject on it and only ever takes over or archives a site that carries that subject or that the deploy reserved for the login. An SSO login outside the group archives the site and keeps its content, a login back in the group restores it. A deploy applies a membership change as well: [tasks/05_site_owners.yml](tasks/05_site_owners.yml) archives every own site whose login is no longer an inventory member and ends that member's sessions."
msgstr ""

msgid "A mesh is IPv4 only, on the underlay as inside the tunnel. Each deploy resolves every endpoint a host dials with ``getent ahostsv4`` on that host, writes the first IPv4 address into ``Endpoint``, measures the path MTU against that address and subtracts the 60-byte IPv4 tunnel header. On an interface that is already up, the deploy sets that MTU on the live link as well. An endpoint name with both an A and an AAAA record therefore always dials over IPv4. A name without an A record, an unreachable resolver, an IPv6 literal endpoint or a host whose only IPv4 address is ``127.0.0.1`` fails the deploy before the interface is rendered; pass the peer’s IPv4 address as ``--endpoint`` instead. A host with an IPv4 address but no IPv4 route to the peer fails at the handshake gate. When the hub’s address changes, redeploy every spoke."
msgstr ""

msgid "A mesh is IPv4 only, on the underlay as inside the tunnel. Each deploy resolves every endpoint a host dials with `getent ahostsv4` on that host, writes the first IPv4 address into `Endpoint`, measures the path MTU against that address and subtracts the 60-byte IPv4 tunnel header. On an interface that is already up, the deploy sets that MTU on the live link as well. An endpoint name with both an A and an AAAA record therefore always dials over IPv4. A name without an A record, an unreachable resolver, an IPv6 literal endpoint or a host whose only IPv4 address is `127.0.0.1` fails the deploy before the interface is rendered; pass the peer's IPv4 address as `--endpoint` instead. A host with an IPv4 address but no IPv4 route to the peer fails at the handshake gate. When the hub's address changes, redeploy every spoke."
msgstr ""

