msgstr "Agente teenindav mudel deklareerib oma kontekstiakna märgistes: `context` ühel `AI_LOCAL_MODELS` sisse- või `services.litellm.remote_models` sissepääs. LiteLLM saadab selle Ollama nagu `num_ctx` ja avaldab selle `model_info.max_input_tokens`, ja maakler kirjutab selle agendikonfiguratsiooni Hermesina `model.context_length` ja OpenClaw `contextWindow`. Ilma selleta. Ollama kärbib agendi päringu oma vaikeaknasse ja agendid võtavad endale oma aknad."

msgid "A model vendor (`flavour: model-vendor`) also lists the agent `runtimes` it serves and its `login_hosts`. A workspace with `model_access: login` adds exactly these hosts to its egress, and only for a runtime the vendor names; in gateway mode they stay closed, and a deny rule of the agent's firewall role removes any of them in both modes; every egress target is compared lowercase and without a trailing dot, and L08 refuses any other spelling. Lint L08 accepts only exact login host names and refuses hosts that serve user content (`claude.ai`, `chatgpt.com`). Codex signed in with a ChatGPT account talks to `chatgpt.com`, which also serves the account's conversations and file uploads, so `openai.yml` does not list it: a login-mode Codex VM works only with an OpenAI API login until the proxy can admit a single path of that host."
