msgstr ""

msgid "A percentage is the only portable way to size against the machine. Docker refuses a `cpus` above the host's core count (`range of CPUs is from 0.01 to N.00`), so `cpus: \"4\"` is a hard failure on a two-core host while `50%` is valid everywhere. `100%` resolves to exactly that ceiling and can never be rejected."
