msgid "A pin the Docker updater (`image` + `version`) and the repository updater (`repository` + `ref`) do not reach names its upstream next to itself:"
msgstr "Dockeri uuendaja tihvt (`image` + `version`) ja hoidla uuendaja (`repository` + `ref`) ei jõua enda kõrval olevate nimedeni:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A platform may refuse a window it considers too small. Hermes requires 64000 tokens and answers `HTTP 500` with \"below the minimum 64,000 required by Hermes Agent\" for anything less, so `web-app-hermes` declares `services.hermes.min_context` and the broker withholds any platform whose minimum the selected model misses: it is absent from `/v1/models` and answers 404, while every other platform keeps serving. Refusing the whole deploy instead would block a pairing that works, since OpenClaw declares no minimum and the broker pulls Hermes into its closure either way. A model that declares no window at all is reported rather than withheld: an agent that does not know its window runs."
msgstr "Platvorm võib keelduda aknast, mida ta peab liiga väikeseks. Hermes vajab 64000 märke ja vastuseid `HTTP 500` koos \"minimaalsest 64,000 nõutud Hermes Agent\" millegi vähema eest. `web-app-hermes` kuulutab `services.hermes.min_context` ja maakler hoiab kinni platvormi, mille minimaalne valitud mudel puudub: `/v1/models` vastuseid 404, Kuigi kõik teised platvormid jätkavad teenimist. Kogu kasutuselevõtust keeldumine blokeeriks sidumise, mis toimib, sest OpenClaw ei deklareeri miinimumi ja maakler tõmbab Hermese igal juhul sulgemisse. Mudel, mis deklareerib, et akent pole üldse, on pigem teatatud kui varjatud: agent, kes ei tea, et tema aken jookseb."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A plug-and-go backup of the local backup tree to an external block device (typically a swappable USB drive). The transfer is hard-link deduplicated against the previous snapshot, so each plug-in yields a complete, browsable point-in-time copy without doubling disk usage."
msgstr "Kohaliku varunduspuu pistik- ja varukoopia välise plokkseadmega (tavaliselt vahetatav USB-draiv). Ülekanne on eelmise hetktõmmise suhtes kõvalingiga deduplitseeritud, nii et iga plugin annab täieliku sirvitava ajahetke koopia ilma ketta kasutamist kahekordistamata."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A plugin MAY ship an appstore release that lags the pinned Nextcloud server major. In that case OCC emits the marker string `is not compatible with this version of the server` and exits non-zero. The pipeline MUST treat this as a non-fatal condition:"
msgstr "Plugin VÕIB saata appstore release, mis jääb kinnine Nextcloud serveri suur. Sellisel juhul väljastab OCC markerstringi `is not compatible with this version of the server` ja väljub nullist. Torujuhtmes tuleb seda käsitleda kui mittesurmavat tingimust:"

msgid "A plugin entry MAY set `mandatory: true`. This inverts the tolerance above: when the plugin is `enabled` for the current deployment but its install result is not `runnable` (incompatible with the pinned server major, or unavailable on the appstore), [02_install.yml](./02_install.yml) aborts the deployment with `ansible.builtin.fail` instead of emitting the skip warning."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A pool of two or more stays a preference because the matrix already narrowed each row to one kind out of it: falling back to the other kind the run allowed is inside what the operator asked for, while failing the row is not. A run whose whole pool is unservable fails rather than leaving the pool."
msgstr "Kahest või enamast koosnev bassein jääb eelistuseks, sest maatriks juba kitsendas iga rea ühte liiki välja: langedes tagasi teise liiki, on lubatud jooks sees, mida operaator küsis, samas kui rida ei ole. Jooks, mille kogu bassein on jälgimatu, pigem ebaõnnestub kui lahkub basseinist."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A pool or token of exactly one kind is read as a human naming it, so the applying step **fails the row instead of substituting** a kind the host can serve. Pinning a kind the runner cannot deliver therefore produces a red job that says nothing about the question."
msgstr "Täpselt ühte liiki bassein või märk loetakse kui inimene, kes nimetab seda, nii et rakendatav samm **rea asendamine ebaõnnestub** Selline, mida peremees saab teenida. Selline, mida jooksja ei suuda pakkuda, tekitab seega punase töö, mis ei ütle midagi küsimuse kohta."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A practical long-term target is:"
msgstr "Praktiline pikaajaline eesmärk on:"

msgid "A pre-flight check probes a host before a deploy changes it and stops the deploy when the host is in a state the deploy cannot recover from on its own: a kernel without its modules, a full disk, a docker object that belongs to another project, a port a host service already holds, or a domain that does not resolve."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A prefix cannot judge the container, so the probe keeps the verdict and the prefix only ever RAISES a timing -- the composed start period is the longest of the two, never the prefix's alone. Lowering it once would have cut a fifteen minute start window down to two."
msgstr "Prefiks ei saa konteinerit hinnata, nii et sond hoiab kohtuotsuse ja prefiks ainult kunagi tõstab ajastust - komponeeritud algusperiood on neist kahest pikim, mitte kunagi eesliide üksi. Selle vähendamine üks kord oleks vähendanud viieteistkümne minuti algusakna kahele."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A prefix does something on the way past -- sending a smoke mail is the only one so far -- and deliberately cannot decide liveness. That separation is what lets a probe stay the single verdict."
msgstr "Eesliide teeb midagi minevikus - suitsukirja saatmine on seni ainus - ja tahtlikult ei saa otsustada elu. See eraldamine on see, mis laseb sondil jääda ainsaks kohtuotsuseks."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A prefix mask leaves a contiguous run of low bits free, so per octet the addresses span exactly ``network_address`` to ``broadcast_address``. The cross product of those four ranges is the network, which makes the octet decomposition exact for any prefix length, aligned or not."
msgstr "Eesliidemask jätab madalate bittide külgneva jooksu vabaks, nii et okteti kohta ulatuvad aadressid täpselt ``network_address`` kuni ``broadcast_address``. Nende nelja vahemiku risttulemus on võrk, mis muudab okteti lagunemise täpseks mis tahes eesliite pikkusele, joondatud või mitte."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A priority entry may pin axes (``web-app-zammad#1@compose+tor``), and the pin rides along into the retrigger: the entry never ran, so the run holds no evidence that the axes it named were the wrong ones. Only the name in front of the axis suffix is resolved against the statuses."
msgstr "Prioriteetne kirje võib tihvtida telgi (``web-app-zammad#1@compose+tor``), ja tihvt sõidab mööda retrigger: sissekanne ei jooksnud kunagi, nii et jooks ei sisalda tõendeid selle kohta, et tema poolt nimetatud teljed olid valed. Olekute suhtes lahendatakse ainult telje sufiksi ees olev nimi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A priority role can fall behind the discovery budget cut in every mode, so the run holds no job for it and :func:`failed_roles` cannot see it — it is neither green nor red, it simply never ran. Carrying it into the retrigger is the only way it ever gets deployed."
msgstr "Prioriteetne roll võib jääda igas režiimis avastamise eelarve kärpimise taha, nii et jooks ei pea selle jaoks tööd ja :func:`failed_roles` See ei ole roheline ega punane, see lihtsalt ei jooksnud. Selle kandmine retriggerisse on ainus viis, kuidas seda kunagi kasutatakse."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A privacy-first foundation for enterprises running AI locally and keeping sensitive data on-prem."
msgstr "Privaatsuse esimene sihtasutus ettevõtetele, kes juhivad AI-d kohapeal ja hoiavad tundlikke andmeid kohapeal."

msgid "A process stuck in `D` cannot be killed and is the host-visible trace of a wedged mount. Only the state field is evaluated; the command name is never retained, so the count can be logged without leaking process command lines. The comm field may itself contain spaces and `)`, so the state is read after the last closing parenthesis rather than by index."
