msgstr "Mõlemad maitsed katavad olekut ja valik loeb ja vastab HTTP-le 422 nende kohal, nii et värav kärbib viivitust, et `services.litellm.router.state_chars` enne küsimist. Theo `laya` maitse jagab fikseeritud sümboolset eelarvet ühe küsimuse valikutes, nii et täpsus langeb maha enne oma korki; siinsed kasutuselevõtud panid sellele käputäis mudeli aliasi, mis on kaugel allpool, kus see on oluline."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Both halves are required: ``tor.enabled`` is the dependency edge, not the port forward, so a client picking the Tor transport from that flag alone dials a port with no HiddenServicePort and no host publish."
msgstr "Vaja on mõlemat poolt: ``tor.enabled`` on sõltuvuse serv, mitte port edasi, nii et klient, kes valib Tor-transpordi sellest lipust üksi, valib pordi, millel pole HiddenServicePort ja host ei avalda."

msgid "Both halves may come through other names. A bare local port number, as ``LDAP.SERVER.PORT``, is left out, because containers pair it with a service name; so are the vhost inputs (``http_port`` and its siblings), which openresty hands to ``proxy_pass`` and swarm ignores, and every value that hands one to the vhost."
