# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Inputs"
msgstr "Sisendid"

msgid "Inputs (env): ``APP_ID``, ``INFINITO_DOMAIN`` (the SPOT for the deployment domain; defined in ``default.env`` and exported by ``scripts/meta/env/load.sh``; the development inventory reads the same env var for the play's ``DOMAIN_PRIMARY``), ``HOSTS_ENTRY_IP`` (address the domains map to; the swarm play sets it from ``INFINITO_SWARM_MGR_IP``)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Inputs (env): ``APP_ID``, ``INV_PATH`` (default ``/tmp/inv/devices.yml``). Optional ``INFINITO_APP_VARIANTS`` (consumed by ``derive_includes``)."
msgstr "Sisendid (env): ``APP_ID``, ``INV_PATH`` (vaikimisi ``/tmp/inv/devices.yml``). Vabatahtlik ``INFINITO_APP_VARIANTS`` (tarbitud ``derive_includes``)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Inputs (env): ``INV_DIR`` — inventory dir holding ``host_vars/*.yml`` (default ``/tmp/inv``)."
msgstr "Sisendid (env): ``INV_DIR`` — inventarihoidla ``host_vars/*.yml`` (vaikimisi ``/tmp/inv``)."

msgid "Inputs (env): ``NFS_IP``, ``MGR_IP``, ``MGR``, ``OUT_PATH`` (default ``/tmp/swarm-nfs-extras.yml``), ``KEY_PATH`` (default ``/tmp/swarm-nfs-admin.key``). A second ed25519 keypair is generated at ``INFINITO_SWARM_BACKUP_KEY`` (SPOT: default.env) and its public half lands in ``users.backup.authorized_keys`` so the DR drill's backup host can pull over the ``user-backup`` ssh-wrapper. The ``applications`` block written into the extras file carries the ``local-2-device`` mount/target/source device paths, which is all the DR drill reads back from it. The deploy-facing overrides, including ``remote-2-local.backup_providers`` (derived per round from ``utils.tests.swarm.backup_repos``), are baked by the matrix orchestrator into the provisioner's host_vars merge (INFINITO_VARS_PAYLOAD), NOT into the extras file: extra-vars replace the whole inventory ``applications`` dict and would strip every generated credential. ``users`` carries the same hazard for the same reason, and its authorized_keys travel the same merge channel. The deploy-facing twin ``<OUT_PATH stem>.deploy.yml`` therefore carries everything except ``applications`` and ``users``, plus ``ansible_become_password``."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Inputs come from the merged application config (``services.<key>.image`` and ``services.<key>.version``). ``image=`` and ``version=`` keyword overrides bypass those values for ad-hoc references (e.g. side-car init containers that do not appear in the services map)."
msgstr "Sisendid pärinevad ühendatud rakenduse seadistusest (``services.<key>.image`` ja ``services.<key>.version``). ``image=`` ja ``version=`` märksõna tühistab need väärtused ad hoc viidete puhul (nt külgvaguni init konteinerid, mida teenuste kaardil ei ole)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Inputs the retrigger reads from the job log rather than the run title."
msgstr "Sisestab retriggeri lugemise töölogist, mitte jooksupealkirjast."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Inputs 🔧"
msgstr "Sisendid 🔧"

msgid "Inside a container the role writes only the namespaced keys: ``net.*``, the IPC keys ``kernel.shm*``, ``kernel.msg*``, ``kernel.sem``, ``kernel.sem_next_id`` and ``fs.mqueue.*``, and the UTS keys ``kernel.hostname`` and ``kernel.domainname``. For every other key it writes neither the live value nor the drop-in, and it prints a skip line. A caller that moves its parameters out of an older file names that file in ``sys_sysctl_retired_files``; the role removes the keys there only after the drop-in holds them and the live value is set."
msgstr ""

msgid "Inside a container the role writes only the namespaced keys: `net.*`, the IPC keys `kernel.shm*`, `kernel.msg*`, `kernel.sem`, `kernel.sem_next_id` and `fs.mqueue.*`, and the UTS keys `kernel.hostname` and `kernel.domainname`. For every other key it writes neither the live value nor the drop-in, and it prints a skip line. A caller that moves its parameters out of an older file names that file in `sys_sysctl_retired_files`; the role removes the keys there only after the drop-in holds them and the live value is set."
msgstr ""

msgid "Inside a play the process boundary is the task: Ansible forks a fresh worker per task, so `_MERGED_APPLICATIONS_CACHE` and `_MERGED_USERS_CACHE` start empty in every worker. `get_merged_applications` therefore also accepts the play-scoped carrier fact `_INFINITO_APPLICATIONS_RENDERED` (payload plus cache key, parked by the constructor stage and again after every role, every nested application load and every persisted token) and serves it when the key matches. The same action parks `_INFINITO_USERS_RENDERED`, which `get_merged_users` serves to templated reads under the applications key plus the token store digest and `inventory_hostname`. See [applications.md](../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/plugins/lookup/applications.md) and [users.md](../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/plugins/lookup/users.md) for the contract."
msgstr ""

