msgid "On a Tor node the node dnsmasq resolves ``.onion`` through Tor's DNSPort and everything else through the clearnet upstream, which is what makes per-app proxy settings unnecessary. It is only reachable on the docker bridge address because docker discards loopback resolvers, and it is absent before docker itself is installed, hence the guard."
msgstr "Tor-sõlmel lahendab sõlm dnsmasq ``.onion`` Tori DNSPorti ja kõige muu kaudu Clearneti ülesvoolu, mis muudab rakendusepõhise puhverserveri seaded tarbetuks. See on kättesaadav ainult dockeri silla aadressile, sest dokker kõrvaldab loopbacki lahendajad ja see puudub enne dockeri enda paigaldamist, seega valvur."

msgid "On a consuming host every consumer uses the mesh URL and the host's key, so no consumer role carries a branch of its own. Inventory provisioning leaves `svc-ai-litellm` out of such a host, and a host that carries it while naming a gateway host fails its deploy. The mesh publish is a compose feature: in swarm the engine does not honour a bind address, so a swarm gateway host does not answer on its mesh address."
msgstr ""

msgid "On a consuming host every consumer uses the mesh URL and the host’s key, so no consumer role carries a branch of its own. Inventory provisioning leaves ``svc-ai-litellm`` out of such a host, and a host that carries it while naming a gateway host fails its deploy. The mesh publish is a compose feature: in swarm the engine does not honour a bind address, so a swarm gateway host does not answer on its mesh address."
msgstr ""

msgid "On a fresh instance the object icons `agent-portal-logo` and `agent-portal-icon` do not exist: before the design import the sign-in page and the header served `/static/img/kix_default.png` as logo and favicon, the fallback of the frontend. The backend console offers `Admin::ObjectIcon::Import` and `Admin::ObjectIcon::SyncAllToFS` only, so `tasks/02_design.yml` can write an icon but not delete one. With `design` switched off again the role therefore imports the images the frontend ships as its seed (`/opt/kix/static/img/kix_start.png`, `kix_start_icon.png`) over the icons it marked, instead of returning to the state without icons. Options: delete the two icons through the backend's Perl API (`Kernel::System::ObjectIcon`) in that case; or keep the seed images."
msgstr ""

