# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "OpenBao auto-unseals on every restart, so deploy and redeploy stay idempotent and no OpenBao-generated key material has to be written back into the inventory. The inventory is the \"existing source of trust\" upstream's caveat asks for."
msgstr "OpenBao käivitab automaatselt igal taaskäivitamisel, nii et installida ja ümber paigutada viibimise idempotentne ja ühtegi OpenBao genereeritud põhimaterjali ei pea loendisse tagasi kirjutama. Inventuur on \"olemasolev usaldusallikas\" Ülemvoolu hoiatus palub."

msgid "OpenBao writes nothing about who read which secret unless an audit device is enabled. OpenBao 2.7 refuses to create audit devices through the API (`cannot enable audit device via API; use declarative, config-based audit device management instead`), so the device is declared in the server configuration. Once any audit device is enabled, OpenBao refuses requests it cannot log. The device therefore writes to the server's stdout, which cannot block. That output reaches the same container log as the rest of the server output. By default OpenBao replaces secret values in audit entries with salted HMACs, so the audit trail does not contain credentials."
msgstr ""

