msgid "The filesystem is a preference unless a human names it 🗄️"
msgstr "Failisüsteem on eelistus, kui inimene seda ei nimeta 🗄️"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The filesystem is the one axis a token built here leaves out. The title states the kind the matrix *assigned*, which a deploy is allowed to fall back from when the host cannot serve it, so the title does not prove what the job ran on. Writing it into a token would also state it as named by a human, which makes it binding (:func:`utils.github.variant.axes.assign`): a retrigger would then fail on the very condition the fallback exists to absorb. The retrigger lets the rotation assign it again and reports what it got. Reading the tokens out of a finished run is what lets a retrigger replay exactly what failed and start the regular line where that run stopped, instead of aggregating to role ids and guessing the rest."
msgstr "Failisüsteem on üks telg, mille siin ehitatud märk välja jätab. Pealkiri ütleb, millist maatriksit *määratud*, mille juurutamisel on lubatud tagasi kukkuda, kui võõrustaja ei saa seda teenindada, nii et pealkiri ei tõesta, mida töö jooksis. Kirjutades selle märgiks, oleks see ka inimese nimega, mis muudab selle siduvaks. (:func:`utils.github.variant.axes.assign`): Retrigger ebaõnnestuks siis just sel tingimusel, et varukoopia on neelamiseks olemas. Retrigger laseb rotatsioonil selle uuesti määrata ja annab teada, mis ta sai. Lõpetatud jooksu märkide lugemine on see, mis võimaldab retriggeril uuesti mängida täpselt seda, mis ebaõnnestus, ja alustada tavalist rida, kus see jooks peatus, selle asemel, et koondada rolli ID-d ja arvata ülejäänud."

msgid "The filter [update_pull_images](../../plugins/filter/update/pull.py) lists every service with an `image` and a `version` that `lookup('applications')` gives a role of `lookup('application_closure', group_names)`, without the shared services another role provides, as the images area of the [Check](#check-) does. A service that declares `custom` runs the `<name>_custom` image its role builds: the playbook skips that image, lists it as built by the role, and pulls the `image` and `version` the service declares, the base of the build. A role that builds an image without declaring `custom` names no built image in its configuration: its declared images are pulled, its built image is neither pulled nor listed. The list holds no sidecar image a compose template takes from a role outside the closure: the redis of a role with an embedded redis or an SSO proxy (`svc-db-redis`), the memcached of OpenProject and Zammad (`svc-db-memcached`), an app-local database its role pins no image for (`svc-db-postgres`, `svc-db-mariadb`), and a local object store. The deploy pulls these small images itself when the host lacks them."
msgstr ""

