msgstr "Paljundusahelas on neli humalat:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The protection rules enforced on `main` are documented in [branch.md](../../tools/github/branch/security.md)."
msgstr "Jõustatud kaitse-eeskirjad `main` dokumenteeritakse [branch.md](../../tools/github/branch/security.md)."

msgid "The protocol is the reason this is a lookup rather than a two-term expression. ``tests/lint/repository/yaml/test_literal_protocol_with_lookup.py`` forbids gluing a literal ``http://`` in front of a value a lookup produced, because the protocol must come from wherever the TLS posture is decided. A container network has no TLS posture: it speaks plaintext by construction. Writing that out per call site meant repeating the same ``# nocheck: literal-protocol-lookup`` next to every one of them, which states a decision nine times instead of once. Holding it here states it once, and the call sites carry no literal protocol for the lint to see."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The provider credential is whatever ``mcp.credential`` declares: ``owner`` names the principal, ``source`` where its secret lives (``token_store`` or the role's own ``credentials``), ``key`` the entry. No provider inherits the administrator's token."
msgstr "Teenusepakkuja mandaat on mis iganes ``mcp.credential`` deklareerib: ``owner`` nimetab printsipaali, ``source`` kus elab tema saladus (``token_store`` või rolli enda ``credentials``), ``key`` sissekanne. Ükski pakkuja ei päri administraatori märki."

msgid "The provider cutover is an inventory change; mailbox data moves with it when the migration switch is on."
