# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The sweep's ordered candidate rows: priority line first, then the regular line, each annotated with the modes it offers and whether it is priority."
msgstr "Pühkimise järjestatud kandidaadiread: prioriteetne rida kõigepealt, seejärel tavaline rida, millest igaüks on märgitud pakutavate režiimidega ja kas see on prioriteet."

msgid "The sweeper of the shared folders and the models removes related files together: an npm `_cacache` index bucket with the content files only it references, a pip `http-v2` entry with its `.body`, a pacman package with its `.sig`, and a Playwright browser directory as a whole; `ms-playwright/.links` stays. A model unit is a whole package directory or file below a tool's folder (`models/libretranslate/<package>`), or an Ollama manifest together with the blobs no other manifest references; the sweeper skips the models folder while a running container mounts it. It never removes a cache root, a directory that is not a unit, or anything outside the cache paths. On a filesystem mounted `noatime` it reads the modification time instead of the access time, and `make cache-status` reports `atime_fallback: true` for that cache."
msgstr ""

msgid "The switch preserves ``auth.json`` and unrelated TOML settings, including MCP servers. TOML formatting is normalized. Redeployment updates the managed settings and key while retaining the selected connection mode. ``CODEX_HOME`` must be unset or point to ``~/.codex``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The switch preserves `auth.json` and unrelated TOML settings, including MCP servers. TOML formatting is normalized. Redeployment updates the managed settings and key while retaining the selected connection mode. `CODEX_HOME` must be unset or point to `~/.codex`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The sync also mirrors the images the CI runner pulls itself, outside every role: the tagged `image` literals of `compose.yml` and `compose/cache.override.yml`, and the image keys of `default.env` listed in `RUNNER_ENV_IMAGES` ([discovery.py](../../../utils/docker/image/discovery.py)). On a GitHub runner, [runner_mirror.py](../../administration/deploy/development/runner_mirror.py) layers a generated compose override that points those services at their mirror, and hands the certificate generator the mirrored init image."
