# [kõne.orchestrator.yml](../../../../../.github/workflows/call-orchestrator.yml)
# võrdleb `github.ref` Samal põhjusel: nimetatakse töövoog pärib helistaja
# ref, mis on `refs/pull/<n>/merge` auks `pull_request` helistaja
# `refs/heads/main` auks `pull_request_target` üks. Theo `ci-orchestrator`
# tööd `entry-pr-change-orchestrate.yml` tarastatud `github.event_name ==
# 'pull_request'`, nii et ref, mida orkestraator sellest helistajast näeb, on
# alati ühinemine ref; avardamine, et tara paneks vaikselt kahvel jookseb
# pearühma.
# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[call-orchestrator.yml](../../../../../.github/workflows/call-orchestrator.yml) compares `github.ref` for the same reason: a called workflow inherits the caller's ref, which is `refs/pull/<n>/merge` for a `pull_request` caller but `refs/heads/main` for a `pull_request_target` one. The `ci-orchestrator` job of `entry-pr-change-orchestrate.yml` is fenced to `github.event_name == 'pull_request'`, so the ref the orchestrator sees from that caller is always the merge ref; widening that fence would silently put fork runs into main's group."
msgstr "[call-orchestrator.yml](../../../../../.github/workflows/call-orchestrator.yml) võrdleb `github.ref` Samal põhjusel: nimetatakse töövoog pärib helistaja ref, mis on `refs/pull/<n>/merge` auks `pull_request` helistaja `refs/heads/main` auks `pull_request_target` üks. Theo `ci-orchestrator` tööd `entry-pr-change-orchestrate.yml` tarastatud `github.event_name == 'pull_request'`, nii et ref, mida orkestraator sellest helistajast näeb, on alati ühinemine ref; avardamine, et tara paneks vaikselt kahvel jookseb pearühma."

